================================================================================
The 1D FFT seed
================================================================================

mac4DSTEM (github.com/mac4DSTEM/mac4DSTEM) at commit
c809679c8ee23a355da6af4f63665aaf64f90d0d:
  mac4DSTEM/Core/Compute/FFT1D.swift (Float radix-2 vDSP FFT).
The public Float API preserves the unnormalised inverse. Length one is handled
explicitly, log2 is computed with integer arithmetic, and nextPow2 rejects
overflow. FFT1DDouble uses the corresponding Double vDSP calls.


================================================================================
The HRTEM filters' method (no code taken)
================================================================================

The average background subtraction and Wiener filters follow R. Kilaas,
"Optimal and near-optimal filters in high-resolution electron microscopy",
J. Microsc. 190 (1998) 45-51, as D. R. G. Mitchell's DigitalMicrograph script
HRTEM_Filter.s v4.0 (2019-11-01) describes them. That script states no licence:
nothing of it is copied. The kit implements the method's steps as the
registration states them (formulas, constants and parameters are method). Its
output has never been compared with DigitalMicrograph.

Tao Ma's hrtem_filter (github.com/matao1984/hrtem_filter, MIT) is an
independent Python implementation, used only as a printed cross-check of the
mask formulas, never copied.


